Skia: defensive null-check for missing stencil attachment in GrRenderTarget::numStencilBits

Under the Flutter linux_drm shell on AMD/Mesa, a draw op with
isStencilEnabled() can target an offscreen FBO that was created without
a stencil attachment (e.g. a saveLayer for BoxShadow blurRadius > 0 or
BackdropFilter, composited above an external DMA-BUF texture). In debug
Skia builds an SkASSERT in GrGLGpu::flushGLState catches this; in release
builds the assertion is compiled out and numStencilBits() null-derefs
getStencilAttachment(), crashing inside libflutter_engine.so when
EmbedderExternalTextureGL::ResolveTextureSkia flushes the pending queue.

Two changes:

  1. GrRenderTarget::numStencilBits returns 0 (instead of crashing) when
     no stencil attachment is bound.
  2. GrGLGpu::flushGLState skips stencil configuration if no attachment
     is bound, so downstream stencil ops become no-ops on the
     stencil-less FBO rather than executing with bogus settings.

This prevents the crash. Visual effects that depend on stencil-based
clipping inside the affected saveLayer may be missing, but BoxShadow
blur itself does not require stencil.

Apply with: patch -p1 -d engine/src < patches/skia-stencil-nullcheck.patch

--- a/flutter/third_party/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/GrRenderTarget.cpp
+++ b/flutter/third_party/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/GrRenderTarget.cpp
@@ -62,5 +62,13 @@
 }

 int GrRenderTarget::numStencilBits(bool useMSAASurface) const {
-    return GrBackendFormatStencilBits(this->getStencilAttachment(useMSAASurface)->backendFormat());
+    // Defensive: in release builds the original code crashed when a draw op
+    // had isStencilEnabled() but the render target lacked a stencil
+    // attachment (an SkASSERT in GrGLGpu::flushGLState caught it in debug
+    // builds only). Returning 0 lets the caller proceed; downstream stencil
+    // ops become no-ops on the stencil-less FBO. Surfaces under the Flutter
+    // linux_drm shell hit this path when a saveLayer/blur (e.g. BoxShadow
+    // blurRadius>0) composites above an external DMA-BUF texture.
+    auto* sa = this->getStencilAttachment(useMSAASurface);
+    return sa ? GrBackendFormatStencilBits(sa->backendFormat()) : 0;
 }
--- a/flutter/third_party/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/gl/GrGLGpu.cpp
+++ b/flutter/third_party/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/gl/GrGLGpu.cpp
@@ -2115,10 +2115,17 @@
     GrGLRenderTarget* glRT = static_cast<GrGLRenderTarget*>(renderTarget);
     GrStencilSettings stencil;
     if (programInfo.isStencilEnabled()) {
-        SkASSERT(glRT->getStencilAttachment(useMultisampleFBO));
-        stencil.reset(*programInfo.userStencilSettings(),
-                      programInfo.pipeline().hasStencilClip(),
-                      glRT->numStencilBits(useMultisampleFBO));
+        // Skip stencil configuration entirely if no attachment is bound —
+        // the SkASSERT below catches this in debug builds, but release
+        // builds previously crashed in numStencilBits's null deref. Seen
+        // under the linux_drm shell when a saveLayer/blur (BoxShadow,
+        // BackdropFilter) targets an FBO whose stencil attachment was
+        // never allocated.
+        if (glRT->getStencilAttachment(useMultisampleFBO)) {
+            stencil.reset(*programInfo.userStencilSettings(),
+                          programInfo.pipeline().hasStencilClip(),
+                          glRT->numStencilBits(useMultisampleFBO));
+        }
     }
     this->flushStencil(stencil, programInfo.origin());
     this->flushScissorTest(GrScissorTest(programInfo.pipeline().isScissorTestEnabled()));
